    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present No. 15 Osprey, a substantial and beautifully maintained three-bedroom, three-bathroom family home, ideally positioned within a quiet cul-de-sac in the highly regarded Barnageeragh Cove development.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, this impressive residence offers spacious, light-filled accommodation thoughtfully designed for modern family living. The ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a generous living room with double doors opening into the bright and expansive open-plan kitchen, dining and family area—an ideal setting for both everyday life and entertaining. A separate utility room and guest WC complete the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including a spacious main bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom and hot press. A particularly valuable feature is the open-plan home office positioned on the bright landing, providing a dedicated and practical workspace for those working or studying from home.\n\nOutside, the property benefits from off-street parking to the front, while the beautifully maintained rear garden is laid mainly in lawn and complemented by a paved patio—perfect for outdoor dining and family enjoyment. A timber-built shed provides useful additional storage.\n\nThe Osprey forms part of the larger Barnageeragh Cove development, a wonderfully family-friendly neighbourhood known for its attractive surroundings, strong community atmosphere and excellent recreational amenities. A children's playground and generous green open space are located just around the corner from No. 15, providing a safe and welcoming setting for families to enjoy.\n\nOne of the area's standout attractions is the beautiful seafront walk leading from Barnageeragh Cove into Skerries town centre. This scenic coastal route offers wonderful views and convenient pedestrian access to the town's sandy beaches, cafés, restaurants, shops and lively harbour area.\n\nSkerries is a thriving coastal town renowned for its strong sense of community, excellent schools and outstanding sporting facilities, with golf, sailing, rugby, GAA, tennis, soccer and cricket clubs all close at hand. The area is well served by both rail and bus connections, while Dublin Airport and the M1 motorway are approximately 12 miles away, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and beyond.\n\nCombining generous accommodation, a peaceful cul-de-sac setting and an exceptional family-friendly location close to the coast, No. 15 Osprey presents a wonderful opportunity to enjoy all that Skerries has to offer."
      },
